---
description: Delightful Finance product and TypeScript constraints
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `.specify/memory/constitution.md` and the active feature artifacts under `specs/`.

- Use strict TypeScript. Do not use `any` or `as` casts; narrow `unknown`, use generics, `satisfies`, and typed adapters.
- Model variants with discriminated unions and required variant-specific data.
- Store money as non-negative integer `amountMinor` plus ISO 4217 `currency`; never use floating-point arithmetic.
- Organizations are tenancy boundaries; financial accounts are ledgers. Enforce org roles and account grants through Jazz permissions.
- Keep Jazz as the local-first durable data/sync layer; user workflows must not wait for network access.
- Add appropriate unit tests and Playwright end-to-end coverage with every feature and production code path; a feature is incomplete until its tests pass.
- Use SvelteKit/Svelte 5, Bits UI, native CSS/CSS variables, XState for multi-step flows, and Paraglide for every visible string. Do not use Tailwind.
- Keep SimpleFIN setup tokens transient; treat Access URLs as secrets and expose them only to org owners/admins.
- Use Jazz audit fields instead of redundant `createdOn`/`updatedOn` fields; keep user-assigned `bookedOn` separate.
